It's not really a play on words; or if it is, the wordplay happened
centuries ago. "moccasin" comes from the Algonquin language, meaning
"shoe"; and the name water moccasin "was conferred upon the snake by
the [early colonial English] settlers [in America], possibly in
reference to the silence with which both the Indians and the snake
progressed when they moved through the grass or the woods."

